WEBVTT

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.260
Eichi...

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:11.200
This is where you were?

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:13.530
Mitsuki!

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:15.300
Answer us!

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:17.160
Mitsuki!

00:00:17.330 --> 00:00:18.530
Where are you?!

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:28.030
<i>Eichi, please hurry and get me.</i>
<i>I'm here. I'll be right here.</i>

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:26.900
<i>I'm begging you!</i>
<i>Please be safe!</i>

00:02:27.460 --> 00:02:28.460
<i>Mitsuki!</i>

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:36.430
<i>Mitsuki!</i>

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:41.100
<i>Mitsuki! Mitsuki!</i>

00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:42.960
<i>Mitsuki!</i>

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:49.200
<i>You idiot!</i>

00:02:57.500 --> 00:03:00.500
<i>This plane will be landing</i>
<i>at Narita Airport shortly.</i>

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:02.030
- Mitsuki...
<i>- Please check your seatbelts once again</i>

00:03:02.060 --> 00:03:03.130
<i>to make sure they</i>
<i>are securely fastened.</i>

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:10.260
I would've never imagined that our trip
to America would be so painful.

00:03:11.130 --> 00:03:11.800
Yes.

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:33.400
Grandma!

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:34.860
She came to the airport
to meet us?

00:03:35.830 --> 00:03:38.400
I contacted her before
we left America.

00:03:44.130 --> 00:03:45.130
Mitsuki.

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:49.100
Grandma...

00:03:50.260 --> 00:03:52.360
Mi...Mitsuki?

00:03:53.530 --> 00:03:55.900
Mrs. Koyama,
this was all my—

00:03:55.930 --> 00:03:56.930
Dr. Wakaoji!

00:03:57.530 --> 00:04:00.830
You told me that going to America
would be good for Mitsuki, did you not?

00:04:01.930 --> 00:04:02.600
Yes.

00:04:02.630 --> 00:04:04.360
And this is the result?

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:08.630
I was opposed to
the trip to America.

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:10.900
But I persuaded myself that

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:14.230
since it would be with the doctor
who Mitsuki trusted, it would be okay.

00:04:15.430 --> 00:04:16.430
I'm sorry.

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:17.230
Umm...

00:04:17.260 --> 00:04:20.730
Right now, Mitsuki needs
all the support she can get.

00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:23.660
So...please...please...
support Mitsuki!

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:26.330
I don't need you to tell me
something I already know.

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:29.560
Let's go, Mitsuki.

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:34.060
I'll take you to the car!

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:35.100
That will not be necessary!

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:38.260
In that case...
I'll deliver her luggage later.

00:04:46.230 --> 00:04:49.330
Dr. Wakaoji, I cannot entrust
her to you any longer.

00:04:49.900 --> 00:04:52.600
From now on, please stay
out of our family's affairs.

00:04:54.730 --> 00:04:57.230
Of course,
I will switch hospitals as well!

00:05:03.860 --> 00:05:06.830
Hey, wait! I'll let you know
if something happens!

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:09.630
Takuto!

00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:29.430
Listen carefully, Mitsuki.
When you—

00:05:29.460 --> 00:05:30.460
Grandma.

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:33.530
I'll never sing again.

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:39.060
I'll give up my dream
of becoming a singer.

00:05:41.060 --> 00:05:44.760
From now on, I will always do
exactly what you tell me to do.

00:05:45.500 --> 00:05:49.800
I-I see. You finally understand.

00:05:50.230 --> 00:05:51.630
I've been telling you
all along, haven't I?

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:54.330
That music only
creates unhappiness.

00:05:54.900 --> 00:05:57.230
You've finally come to
understand that, haven't you?

00:05:57.960 --> 00:05:59.800
It was exactly as I told you,
wasn't it?

00:06:00.930 --> 00:06:03.160
Yes, it really was.

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:30.560
I can't watch her any longer.

00:06:31.030 --> 00:06:31.700
I...

00:06:31.930 --> 00:06:35.030
Did she really mean it when
she said she'd never sing again?

00:06:35.530 --> 00:06:36.830
And also, Takuto...

00:06:39.460 --> 00:06:41.460
Those backward letters
won't go away.

00:06:42.060 --> 00:06:43.960
If things continue this way,
Mitsuki will really—

00:06:44.230 --> 00:06:48.300
That's right, she'll leave this world
before she's able to live out her lifespan.

00:06:50.860 --> 00:06:52.000
Hello!

00:06:52.030 --> 00:06:54.430
How are you,
Mero and Takuto?

00:06:55.460 --> 00:06:58.130
You seem to be worrying about
unimportant things as usual.

00:06:59.460 --> 00:07:02.560
Unimportant?!
What do you know?!

00:07:02.930 --> 00:07:03.930
Takuto!

00:07:03.960 --> 00:07:09.000
Izumi, don't stick your nose into this.
This is Green Onion Ramen's work.

00:07:09.130 --> 00:07:11.160
It has nothing to
do with you, Izumi!

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:12.700
Work, huh?

00:07:13.100 --> 00:07:15.560
But, to be blunt, it's more
than just work for you

00:07:15.600 --> 00:07:17.900
when it comes to that girl,
isn't it?

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:20.660
That's why I, as a Death Spirit
with more experience,

00:07:20.700 --> 00:07:22.130
have come to give you
some advice.

00:07:22.560 --> 00:07:23.560
Advice?

00:07:24.030 --> 00:07:27.800
That's right. I promise not to tell
the Division Chief of Death Spirits,

00:07:27.830 --> 00:07:31.500
but you should just reap her life
and store it somewhere.

00:07:31.660 --> 00:07:32.660
What did you say?!

00:07:32.860 --> 00:07:34.800
You jerk, stop saying
whatever you want!

00:07:34.830 --> 00:07:38.030
Yeah! That goes against
the duties of a Death Spirit!

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:39.200
As a general rule, yes.

00:07:39.860 --> 00:07:44.600
But, in Mitsuki's current state,
she's just like a corpse waiting to die.

00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:47.460
If she were to continue
living until spring,

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:49.530
don't you think it would
be just too pitiful?

00:07:49.960 --> 00:07:51.700
How pitiful.

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:54.860
Well, see you.

00:07:55.630 --> 00:07:57.630
If there's anything I can do to help,
just let me know.

00:07:58.330 --> 00:07:59.660
Bye, Mero.

00:08:01.130 --> 00:08:03.100
See you around.

00:08:04.200 --> 00:08:06.260
You jerk.
Stop messing with us!

00:08:06.300 --> 00:08:07.960
But Takuto...

00:08:08.730 --> 00:08:12.400
With Mitsuki as she is now...
it may be just as Izumi says.

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:21.660
I don't know what to do anymore.
What can we do at this point?

00:08:32.600 --> 00:08:33.600
How is she?

00:08:34.130 --> 00:08:35.800
Hmm... Well...

00:08:38.500 --> 00:08:40.430
I really can't say
anything conclusive

00:08:40.460 --> 00:08:42.000
until I have seen the results
of the extensive tests.

00:08:42.260 --> 00:08:43.260
I see.

00:08:44.030 --> 00:08:48.700
Mitsuki, I need to speak with the doctor,
so please wait outside.

00:08:49.300 --> 00:08:50.930
All right.

00:09:01.030 --> 00:09:03.030
She's a very
sweet granddaughter,

00:09:03.060 --> 00:09:04.530
listening to what
her grandmother tells her.

00:09:04.960 --> 00:09:06.130
You're too kind.

00:09:16.930 --> 00:09:18.160
I'm really sorry!

00:09:18.400 --> 00:09:19.960
You really did it this time!

00:09:20.960 --> 00:09:22.800
I don't intend to
make any excuses.

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:25.560
This is make or break time
for Full Moon!

00:09:25.860 --> 00:09:27.460
What in the world
are you thinking,

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:28.960
giving her time off
on your own authority!

00:09:32.900 --> 00:09:35.800
Can you really call yourself
a professional manager?

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:42.630
You can go home for today.
I will contact you later.

00:09:50.760 --> 00:09:51.430
<i>What?!</i>

00:09:51.460 --> 00:09:53.260
<i>Full Moon cancelled?</i>

00:09:53.500 --> 00:09:54.830
<i>That's right.</i>

00:09:54.960 --> 00:09:56.700
<i>She was supposed</i>
<i>to be today's guest,</i>

00:09:56.730 --> 00:09:58.530
<i>but she cancelled</i>
<i>because of health issues.</i>

00:09:58.760 --> 00:10:00.000
<i>That's unfortunate!</i>

00:10:00.230 --> 00:10:02.430
<i>I hope she comes back</i>
<i>to work soon!</i>

00:10:02.460 --> 00:10:03.130
<i>Yes.</i>

00:10:03.160 --> 00:10:04.300
<i>The other guests are...</i>

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:06.800
<i>Madoka Wakamatsu,</i>
<i>Shonen Drill...</i>

00:10:15.230 --> 00:10:16.400
Dr. Wakaoji...

00:10:17.300 --> 00:10:18.300
Welcome home.

00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:22.000
It makes me sad that
you didn't consult me.

00:10:22.930 --> 00:10:23.930
I'm sorry.

00:10:24.400 --> 00:10:26.330
It's true that the only
option right now is for

00:10:26.360 --> 00:10:30.560
Mitsuki to take some time off because
she isn't healthy enough to work.

00:10:31.560 --> 00:10:33.000
But you could have at least
said something to me.

00:10:33.260 --> 00:10:37.260
No. I think it was better that
I made that decision alone.

00:10:38.630 --> 00:10:42.030
My office may fire me,

00:10:42.060 --> 00:10:45.530
since I gave our number one idol
time off without permission.

00:10:46.260 --> 00:10:50.330
Hopefully it will end with me being fired
and not turn into a liability issue.

00:10:50.860 --> 00:10:54.360
That's why it's better that you're
not involved in this, Dr. Wakaoji.

00:10:58.230 --> 00:11:00.660
It would make me very angry if you
really meant what you just said.

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:01.930
Huh?

00:11:02.230 --> 00:11:06.030
I am Mitsuki's main doctor
as well as Full Moon's producer.

00:11:06.960 --> 00:11:10.260
So you, as her manager,
and I share a common destiny.

00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:12.030
Dr. Wakaoji...

00:11:12.830 --> 00:11:15.060
Don't try to shoulder
all the responsibilities.

00:11:16.060 --> 00:11:17.430
Please depend on me more.

00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:26.000
I wasn't able to do anything.

00:11:27.730 --> 00:11:32.030
Even though I had
decided to support Mitsuki

00:11:32.060 --> 00:11:34.930
not only as a singer
but also as a girl.

00:11:35.700 --> 00:11:39.200
Not just as a manager who is
in charge of her schedule,

00:11:39.230 --> 00:11:43.760
but as someone who truly cares about
what is going on in Mitsuki's heart.

00:11:44.500 --> 00:11:45.560
But I...

00:11:46.400 --> 00:11:48.260
I wasn't able to do anything.

00:11:49.060 --> 00:11:53.030
Even now when Mitsuki is in
such distress, I can't do anything.

00:11:53.960 --> 00:12:00.360
I thought I understood Mitsuki well.
But I'm not even able to help at all.

00:12:02.460 --> 00:12:05.700
Don't say anymore.
Don't blame yourself like that.

00:12:42.560 --> 00:12:43.830
Thank you for the meal.

00:12:44.230 --> 00:12:45.600
Huh? You're already done?

00:12:46.100 --> 00:12:48.130
Mitsuki, finish what's
on your plate.

00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:50.060
I'm sorry.

00:12:54.660 --> 00:12:56.100
Umm... Mitsuki?

00:13:00.760 --> 00:13:03.660
I wonder if I didn't
season it well.

00:13:16.930 --> 00:13:18.100
Wait a second!

00:13:18.230 --> 00:13:19.230
Why?!

00:13:19.260 --> 00:13:20.300
Because I said so!

00:13:21.160 --> 00:13:23.860
But Mitsuki said she
was giving up singing!

00:13:24.230 --> 00:13:25.700
She's getting
weaker and weaker.

00:13:25.830 --> 00:13:27.600
We need to report this
to those two!

00:13:29.360 --> 00:13:33.230
I can't believe that she meant it
when she said that.

00:13:34.700 --> 00:13:36.700
There's no way she would
be able to give up singing!

00:13:37.560 --> 00:13:38.560
Takuto...

00:13:39.200 --> 00:13:42.300
If we tell her manager
and Wakaoji right now,

00:13:42.330 --> 00:13:43.900
it would just
worry them more.

00:13:44.600 --> 00:13:46.630
Let's monitor the situation
a little bit longer. Please!

00:13:48.130 --> 00:13:49.130
All right.

00:13:49.860 --> 00:13:54.000
But...I wonder if the day will really
come when Mitsuki sings again.

00:14:21.560 --> 00:14:24.000
Mitsuki, are you cold?

00:14:25.100 --> 00:14:25.760
No.

00:14:26.100 --> 00:14:28.600
You should lie down a little
when we get home.

00:14:29.830 --> 00:14:30.500
Okay.

00:14:33.430 --> 00:14:35.760
Is there anything you want?

00:14:36.200 --> 00:14:38.360
No, nothing in particular.

00:14:40.130 --> 00:14:41.160
I see.

00:14:49.230 --> 00:14:52.560
Full Moon wasn't on TV
the other day.

00:14:53.030 --> 00:14:55.000
Maybe she's taking time off
from work again?

00:14:55.360 --> 00:14:57.230
No, it might be a new kind
of promotion tactic.

00:14:57.260 --> 00:14:59.360
There's no way
it's a promotion tactic!

00:14:59.900 --> 00:15:02.660
There's no way that girl would
take a break from singing

00:15:02.700 --> 00:15:04.330
to use such a feeble tactic!

00:15:04.700 --> 00:15:05.800
What's up with her?

00:15:06.060 --> 00:15:07.060
How weird.

00:15:07.100 --> 00:15:08.100
Hey, let's go.

00:15:09.460 --> 00:15:10.130
<i>That's right!</i>

00:15:10.360 --> 00:15:14.660
<i>There's no way that dumb Full Moon</i>
<i>would stop singing for no reason!</i>

00:15:14.900 --> 00:15:17.930
<i>It's Full Moon who's always</i>
<i>singing with carefree abandon!</i>

00:15:18.230 --> 00:15:18.900
I know!

00:15:19.060 --> 00:15:20.760
Something happened!

00:15:28.230 --> 00:15:28.900
What is that?

00:15:29.230 --> 00:15:30.360
Oh... Ma'am.

00:15:30.600 --> 00:15:32.430
Is that for Mitsuki?

00:15:32.630 --> 00:15:33.300
Yes.

00:15:33.500 --> 00:15:36.330
Mitsuki doesn't have
any appetite these days!

00:15:36.430 --> 00:15:41.330
I thought maybe she would eat
her favorite taiyaki from Shunpudo.

00:15:42.960 --> 00:15:43.630
I'll do it.

00:15:44.160 --> 00:15:44.830
Huh?

00:15:44.860 --> 00:15:46.230
I will bring them to her.

00:15:46.700 --> 00:15:47.360
Huh?!

00:15:49.200 --> 00:15:50.560
Umm... Ma'am...

00:15:57.860 --> 00:15:59.400
Madam has changed.

00:15:59.800 --> 00:16:02.460
I wonder if there's going to be
a natural disaster of some sort.

00:16:18.460 --> 00:16:19.460
Mitsuki!

00:16:24.130 --> 00:16:25.130
Mitsuki.

00:16:27.030 --> 00:16:28.030
Grandma...

00:16:30.360 --> 00:16:32.260
Ms. Tanaka bought
these for you.

00:16:33.060 --> 00:16:37.960
She's worried about you because you
haven't been eating much these days.

00:16:39.000 --> 00:16:44.200
Thank you very much.
But I'm not hungry.

00:16:45.730 --> 00:16:46.730
I see.

00:17:06.360 --> 00:17:10.130
How is she?
The test results are in, aren't they?

00:17:10.400 --> 00:17:13.830
It's a very difficult
situation after all.

00:17:14.130 --> 00:17:16.130
I believe that we should
go ahead and operate.

00:17:16.860 --> 00:17:17.530
Huh?

00:17:17.560 --> 00:17:18.230
Operate?

00:17:18.560 --> 00:17:21.260
Umm... Will that affect
the vocal cords?

00:17:21.830 --> 00:17:23.900
Yes, I have to tell you that

00:17:23.930 --> 00:17:26.330
there is definitely a possibility
that she will lose her voice.

00:17:31.200 --> 00:17:35.060
Doctor, if she has the operation,
she will be saved, right?

00:17:35.100 --> 00:17:35.760
I won't do it.

00:17:38.860 --> 00:17:43.030
I absolutely won't do it.
I won't have the operation.

00:17:43.930 --> 00:17:46.430
I don't want to lose my voice.

00:17:46.800 --> 00:17:51.000
M-Mitsuki! Do you understand
what you're saying?!

00:17:52.530 --> 00:17:54.660
If you don't have the operation,
you will...

00:17:54.700 --> 00:17:56.500
I don't care what
happens to me.

00:17:56.630 --> 00:17:57.300
Huh?

00:17:58.660 --> 00:18:00.060
I don't care anymore.

00:18:04.460 --> 00:18:07.330
Hey! Do you really mean
what you just said?!

00:18:07.500 --> 00:18:08.730
H-Hey, Takuto!

00:18:09.000 --> 00:18:11.100
Until just recently,
you were saying that

00:18:11.130 --> 00:18:13.730
you would live the short life
you were given to the fullest!

00:18:14.160 --> 00:18:15.560
But now you're saying

00:18:15.600 --> 00:18:17.800
you will never sing again
and that you don't care!

00:18:18.100 --> 00:18:19.730
That's not like you, Mitsuki!

00:18:20.060 --> 00:18:21.400
Takuto, calm down!

00:18:22.460 --> 00:18:23.460
Damn this!

00:18:26.730 --> 00:18:33.460
Why?! Why won't you sing?
You loved singing so much!

00:18:35.460 --> 00:18:40.500
I'll transform you as many
times as you want!

00:18:45.430 --> 00:18:46.560
She's not transforming!

00:18:47.000 --> 00:18:48.060
No way!

00:18:55.100 --> 00:18:56.100
Why?

00:18:56.460 --> 00:18:58.430
Unless Mitsuki has the desire,

00:18:58.460 --> 00:19:02.030
we won't be able to transform her
with our Death Spirit powers.

00:19:03.100 --> 00:19:04.100
Mitsuki!

00:19:04.260 --> 00:19:07.730
I was able contact a different hospital.
Let's hurry over there.

00:19:13.560 --> 00:19:14.560
Wait!

00:19:22.730 --> 00:19:24.460
<i>She's not herself right now.</i>

00:19:25.230 --> 00:19:27.930
<i>The real Mitsuki could</i>
<i>never give up singing.</i>

00:19:29.460 --> 00:19:33.130
<i>For people who sing,</i>
<i>singing is a testimony of life itself.</i>

00:19:34.160 --> 00:19:36.900
<i>I will make her like singing again.</i>

00:19:38.330 --> 00:19:40.900
<i>Giving up on singing is not something</i>
<i>that you can do so easily.</i>

00:19:41.500 --> 00:19:43.900
<i>I know that best.</i>

00:19:46.160 --> 00:19:47.200
Ow...

00:19:53.160 --> 00:19:54.830
What was that just now?

00:20:02.100 --> 00:20:03.330
I agree.

00:20:03.960 --> 00:20:06.760
This is definitely a condition
that requires surgery.

00:20:07.160 --> 00:20:09.000
That is your opinion too?

00:20:09.660 --> 00:20:12.830
We've gotten the same opinion
from various hospitals.

00:20:13.900 --> 00:20:17.300
It would be great if one could operate
without injuring the vocal cords,

00:20:17.330 --> 00:20:18.760
but that is extremely difficult.

00:20:19.630 --> 00:20:22.030
I understand that Dr. Lon Herberd
is developing

00:20:22.060 --> 00:20:26.530
a new operating technique in America,
but it's still unavailable in Japan.

00:20:27.360 --> 00:20:31.460
In America? With that technique,
the vocal cords wouldn't be injured?

00:20:31.760 --> 00:20:34.900
No, though it is
not 100% certain yet.

00:20:35.500 --> 00:20:40.760
But in Japan, we just don't
have the facilities or the surgeons.

00:20:41.130 --> 00:20:45.230
Of those that I know of,
I believe Dr. Wakaoji

00:20:45.260 --> 00:20:48.760
at Tanemura General Hospital
is knowledgeable about this.

00:20:51.400 --> 00:20:53.960
Dr. Wakaoji?

00:20:54.500 --> 00:20:58.930
That's right. There is no better
doctor practicing in that field.

00:20:59.400 --> 00:21:02.560
If you'd like, I'd be happy to
write a letter of introduction.

00:21:03.760 --> 00:21:09.960
Jeez, where did that Takuto go?
I just assumed he was behind us.

00:21:11.700 --> 00:21:14.860
<i>My throat...</i>
<i>I don't want to lose my voice.</i>

00:21:17.100 --> 00:21:17.760
<i>Because...</i>

00:21:18.300 --> 00:21:24.530
<i>Because if I don't continue to call</i>
<i>out to him, Eichi won't turn around.</i>

00:23:07.000 --> 00:23:10.330
Takuto, just what do we do?
She's...

00:23:10.430 --> 00:23:13.860
That can't be! There's no way
she'll stay like this!

00:23:13.900 --> 00:23:16.300
But her appetite
is even affected

00:23:16.330 --> 00:23:18.130
now that she knows she'll
never see Eichi again.

00:23:19.460 --> 00:23:20.460
Wait a second!

00:23:20.500 --> 00:23:23.900
Was that Madoka Wakamatsu
that I saw going in to the house?

00:23:24.360 --> 00:23:25.660
What is going on?!

00:23:26.730 --> 00:23:30.560
Next time on Full Moon:
"A Sympathetic Heart."

00:23:31.030 --> 00:23:32.060
- Look forward to it!
- Look forward to it!
